.TH FERDIM 1 "2026-10-21" "ferdim 1.3.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ferdim \- dynamic, self-tuning download manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferdim
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBFerDim\fR is a segmented, self-tuning download manager for Linux. Its
engine opens up to 32 parallel connections per file and continuously
calibrates the connection count to saturate either the local line or the
remote server, whichever ceiling is reachable. Downloads are crash-safe
(sparse part files with periodic metadata checkpoints and ETag/If-Range
validation), adapt gracefully to server throttling (HTTP 429/503), and
resume after restarts. A daemon exposes a Unix-socket JSON-RPC API plus a
token-protected localhost HTTP API; front-ends include this CLI, a web UI
(http://127.0.0.1:8378) and a GTK 4 application. A Firefox WebExtension
hands browser downloads and detected media over to the daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI add " URL"
Queue a download. Options:
.B \-o " FILE"
output name,
.B \-d " DIR"
target directory,
.BI \-n " N"
connection count (1\(en32),
.BI \-H " \"Header: Value\""
extra HTTP header (repeatable),
.B \-c " COOKIE"
Cookie header,
.B \-r " REFERER"
Referer header,
.BI \-u / \-p " USER/PASS"
HTTP Basic authentication,
.BI \-\-proxy " URL"
proxy,
.BI \-\-limit " RATE"
per-job speed limit (e.g. 2MB),
.B \-k
skip TLS verification,
.B \-\-wait
follow progress until completion.
.TP
.BI list
Show the queue.
.TP
.BI pause " ID|all" \ ( resume ", " cancel ", " restart ", " remove )
Control jobs; \fBremove \-\-delete\-files\fR also discards partial data.
.TP
.BI limit " RATE"
Global speed limit (\fB0\fR disables).
.TP
.BI turbo " on|off|status"
Toggle maximum-power defaults (32 links, unlimited speed, 8 concurrent jobs).
.TP
.BI config " [\-\-set JSON]"
Show or change settings (segments, concurrency, scheduler window, language).
.TP
.BI daemon
Run the RPC/HTTP daemon in the foreground (normally started via the
\fBferdim.service\fR systemd user unit).
.TP
.BI web
Open the web UI in the default browser.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ferdim/
Socket, token, PID, queue state and job metadata.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ferdim/config.json
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ferdim/ferdim-extension.zip
Unsigned Firefox extension bundle; sign once with
.BR web-ext (1)
or load temporarily via about:debugging.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://github.com/proxy-turkey/ferdim
.SH AUTHOR
Enes Aksu <eaksu@pm.me>
